static - 
	static means the member belongs to the class rather than to individual objects.
	other - The static keyword indicates that a member belongs to the class rather than individual objects. Static variables have one shared copy across all objects, and static methods can be called without creating an object. Static methods cannot directly access instance members or use this and super. Static methods are resolved at compile time, so they participate in method hiding rather than runtime method overriding.
